{"author":{"id":"038d65070aa747b6bc9d50939fa697ec871a40ed259db54429b255bbef2581d6"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1792308554,"nonce":"ArxeRRUXjpVnY0paS0mKF7H5kWo=","title":"Keep an open file's editor alive when other tabs open and close","message":"Workbench.editorCard rebuilds every code-editor whenever the open list changes, so opening or closing a tab loses the other files' undo history, scroll and caret (buffers survive in Workbench.buffers). Switching tabs does not rebuild. Keep each file's editor mounted while it is open, adding and removing only the one that changed.","files":null}]}